                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It took me 37mins to finish this game, on my first go.\nAnd I wan't particularly good at it.\nAnd I accidentally let it run while I was typing something on another screen.\n\nPros:\n- There are some cool game mechanics.\n- The music isn't too annoying to listen to for the 37mins it took me to finish the game.\n\nCons:\n- Walking around is very difficult, it seems to lag a little, and you can't tell when you are trying to walk into a space which is occupied by the edge of another object (invisible walls that shouldn't be there).\n- It's extremely hard to see what's happening in this game, or where the aim bar is at.\n- There is a significant time delay between throwing snowballs, and you can't turn after you start winding up the snowball, which is frustrating because half the time I accidentally bumped a direction button while trying to throw one, or accidentally started to throw one while I was still trying to move into position.\n- The game doesn't pause or stop between levels, and doesn't pause when you have the game minimised.\n- The game seems to freeze when you reach the end, before displaying the message telling you that you have won. I almost quit and restarted the game when this happened, as I didn't expect to have reached the end after 37mins.",
